WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.840
Hello, I'm Camille.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:06.438
If you're the victim of a scam, there's no need to feel ashamed: scammers are professionals.

3
00:00:06.788 --> 00:00:09.972
What matters is acting fast. Here are four steps.

4
00:00:10.672 --> 00:00:11.992
Step one: block.

5
00:00:12.342 --> 00:00:21.686
Block your card straight away, using your banking app or the number on the back of your card. In the UK, you can also call 159 to reach your bank safely.

6
00:00:22.036 --> 00:00:26.204
If you made a transfer, call your bank immediately to try to stop it.

7
00:00:26.554 --> 00:00:29.522
Then change your passwords, starting with your email.

8
00:00:30.222 --> 00:00:32.582
Step two: keep the evidence.

9
00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.396
Don't delete anything: messages, emails, phone numbers.

10
00:00:36.746 --> 00:00:38.098
Take screenshots.

11
00:00:38.448 --> 00:00:42.408
And write down the date, the time, and what you were told.

12
00:00:43.108 --> 00:00:45.148
Step three: report it.

13
00:00:45.498 --> 00:00:54.418
In the UK, contact Report Fraud on 0300 123 2040, or at reportfraud.police.uk.

14
00:00:54.768 --> 00:01:03.976
In the US, report it to the FTC at ReportFraud.ftc.gov, and online crime to the FBI at IC3.gov.

15
00:01:04.676 --> 00:01:06.844
Step four: ask for a refund.

16
00:01:07.194 --> 00:01:11.186
Write to your bank, without delay, to dispute the operations you didn't authorise.

17
00:01:11.536 --> 00:01:14.216
In the UK, you have up to thirteen months to claim.

18
00:01:14.566 --> 00:01:18.430
In the US, report it within sixty days of the statement that shows it.

19
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:24.292
If your bank refuses, make a formal complaint, then contact the ombudsman or the regulator.

20
00:01:24.992 --> 00:01:26.536
You can also get help.

21
00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:32.046
In the UK, Victim Support listens on 08 08 16 89 111, day and night.

22
00:01:32.396 --> 00:01:39.732
In the US, the AARP Fraud Watch Network helpline answers on 877-908-3360, for everyone.

23
00:01:40.082 --> 00:01:45.322
Finally, beware of anyone who promises to recover your money for a fee: that's another scam.

24
00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:48.766
Remember: distrust is the mother of safety.

25
00:01:49.116 --> 00:01:51.916
That was Camille, for WhitePaw. See you soon!
